# FE-01 — Content Security Policy and transport hardening for the static
# storefront and admin console.
#
# helmet sets a CSP on API responses, but the CSP that matters is the one on the
# HTML documents themselves — and those are served by Netlify, which applied no
# policy at all. This file is Netlify's mechanism for that.
#
#
# WHY RAZORPAY IS A WILDCARD, AND WHY form-action ADMITS IT
#
# Razorpay Checkout is not one origin. It loads checkout.razorpay.com, frames
# api.razorpay.com, talks to lumberjack.razorpay.com for telemetry, and uses
# regional and CDN subdomains that are not documented and can change. Naming
# them individually means a payment fails one day with an opaque console error
# and nobody connects it to a header.
#
# form-action originally read `'self'`, which is stricter — and I verified in a
# real browser that it genuinely blocks cross-origin form POSTs. This project
# uses the modal integration (`new Razorpay(opts).open()`), which renders in an
# iframe and is therefore unaffected, so 'self' would PROBABLY have been fine.
#
# "Probably" is the wrong standard for a payment path. Razorpay already holds
# script-src and frame-src grants, meaning it can already execute code in this
# page — refusing it a form POST buys no real protection, while getting it wrong
# means a customer picks their bank, the redirect is silently blocked, and the
# order fails with nothing to diagnose. The restriction is dropped where it is
# theatre and kept everywhere it bites.
#
# NOTE: connect-src names the API host explicitly. If the API ever moves to a
# custom domain (api.chakrashri.com), THIS LINE MUST CHANGE or every request
# from the storefront is blocked.
#
# Chart.js is self-hosted (see admin.html), so cdnjs is deliberately absent
# from script-src — one fewer third-party origin able to run code on the admin
# console.
#
# WHY 'unsafe-inline' IS STILL PRESENT, stated plainly rather than hidden:
# both pages carry ~200 inline onclick attributes and a large inline <style>
# block. A policy without 'unsafe-inline' would break the site outright. The
# honest sequence is: ship a real policy now, which closes external script
# injection, framing, form hijacking and plugin embedding today; then migrate
# the inline handlers to delegated listeners and tighten script-src to
# 'self' plus a nonce. The remaining gap is documented, not pretended away.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://checkout.razorpay.com https://*.razorpay.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://chakrashri-api.onrender.com https://*.razorpay.com; frame-src https://*.razorpay.com; form-action 'self' https://*.razorpay.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(self "https://checkout.razorpay.com"), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The HTML itself must never be cached hard — a stale index.html is what the
# site_settings content_version handshake exists to work around, and a
# long-lived cache here would defeat it.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/admin.html
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# The build-time catalog snapshot (scripts/generate-catalog-snapshot.js), which
# index.html renders its first paint from while the API is still waking.
#
# The numbers are chosen for that job specifically. max-age=300 means a shopper
# clicking through several pages pays no network cost at all after the first
# one. stale-while-revalidate is the part that matters: for a day after that
# five minutes, the browser serves the cached copy INSTANTLY and refreshes it in
# the background, so a returning visitor never waits on this file either — and
# a stale copy is corrected within seconds by the live API fetch regardless.
#
# It is only ever display data. Price and stock are re-checked server-side at
# add-to-cart and at checkout, which is what makes caching it this hard safe.
/catalog.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
